e last digit of $12a+11.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $b=12a+11.$ Note that $b$ is positive. Now, let ${d}_{3},$ ${d}_{2},$ and ${d}_{1}$ be the last three digits of the number $b:$ \n\n$$\nb=…{d}_{3}{d}_{2}{d}_{1}\n$$\n\nThen, $b$ can be written in expanded form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =⋯+100{d}_{3}+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} \\\\  & =10(⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the residue of $b$ modulo $10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ≡10(⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0\\cdot (⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${d}_{1}$ is the last digit of $b.$\n\nFinally, since $b=12a+11,$ and \n\n$$\n12≡2,\\,11≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 12a+11 & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 2a+1 & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression that gives the last digit of $12a+11$ is the following:\n\n$$\n2a+1\\,\\text{mod}\\,10\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ffdfb29-a3d2-5a7a-868c-21eab8965922" :knowledge-point/title "Modular Residues of Positive Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0015065c-e020-549d-8843-ecb2b21a3462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0015065c-e020-549d-8843-ecb2b21a3462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412259} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41cffe8-3aaa-5190-832f-40d305241d5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da9aaccf-ed58-5942-8a55-f387c4ff158b" :question/math-academy-id "q-213027" :question/problem "$14\\text{ mod }6=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The residue of $14$ modulo $6$ is the integer $0\\le r<6$ such that\n\n$$\n14≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $14$ as an integer multiple of $6,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $14≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ because\n\n$$\n14=2\\cdot 6+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $14$ modulo $6$ is $2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & ≡14-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡14-2\\cdot 6 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡14-12 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $14$ modulo $6$ is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ffdfb29-a3d2-5a7a-868c-21eab8965922" :knowledge-point/title "Modular Residues of Positive Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4818c49a-4b28-56a1-84b2-20b5cc1b77cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4818c49a-4b28-56a1-84b2-20b5cc1b77cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412292} :answer-field/id #uuid "0905d27b-bf64-570e-8e3a-3ea2e09cbd45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7119d9e9-8c81-54dd-a944-533c5aa1aed1" :question/math-academy-id "q-213046" :question/problem "$27\\text{ mod }4=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The residue of $27$ modulo $4$ is the integer $0\\le r<4$ such that\n\n$$\n27≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $27$ as an integer multiple of $4,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $27≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ because\n\n$$\n27=6\\cdot 4+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $27$ modulo $4$ is $3.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the subtraction property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27 & ≡27-0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡27-6\\cdot 4 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡27-24 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\  & ≡3 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $27$ modulo $4$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152056 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70cef00-bf25-5423-85ac-2d3a44c68f35" :knowledge-point/title "Modular Residues of Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2108e1-8c03-51d5-809d-d47e269ec3c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2108e1-8c03-51d5-809d-d47e269ec3c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412323} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b90a83-101c-5227-b1b7-407300b1fd00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d645eda-2214-5faa-a63b-2fee859e4238" :question/math-academy-id "q-213076" :question/problem "$-7\\text{ mod }2=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The residue of $-7$ modulo $2$ is the integer $0\\le r<2$ such that\n\n$$\n-7≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-7$ as an integer multiple of $2,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-7≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$ because\n\n$$\n-7=(-4)\\cdot 2+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-7$ modulo $2$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & ≡-7+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2) \\\\  & ≡-7+4\\cdot 2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2) \\\\  & ≡-7+8 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2) \\\\  & ≡1 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-7$ modulo $2$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152056 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70cef00-bf25-5423-85ac-2d3a44c68f35" :knowledge-point/title "Modular Residues of Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "452e4778-8d1c-58fb-8493-02220c8324c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "452e4778-8d1c-58fb-8493-02220c8324c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412291} :answer-field/id #uuid "cadd8c20-4787-5c4e-9b19-fc516ac97d48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a2135af-f11d-5278-a560-c7cd73d93e86" :question/math-academy-id "q-213089" :question/problem "$-54\\text{ mod }7=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is the integer $0\\le r<7$ such that\n\n$$\n-54≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-54$ as an integer multiple of $7,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-54≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ because\n\n$$\n-54=(-8)\\cdot 7+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is $2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-54 & ≡-54+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-54+8\\cdot 7 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-54+56 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡2 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-54$ modulo $7$ is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152057 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a090bd2-cdb1-5680-81bc-3cb36de126c4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Last Few Digits of a Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7a2e7d-a7f7-51a9-b5d1-e6a08a235d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412287} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b6f99d-95c5-5d1d-a379-204d9be49203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412311} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc79298-8b18-5c41-ab31-d5b786527dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412319} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf57528-f936-530c-ae91-0ae767897668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5a+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfc79298-8b18-5c41-ab31-d5b786527dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412319} :answer-field/id #uuid "1829be2b-0030-55a2-ac4d-e2351dae6d32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080ba340-0c2e-55b9-adbc-0e8561a2fd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\,÷" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412266} {:answer/id #uuid "1915435a-1ef7-53cf-