ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3a0e9ee-2041-5135-bc63-3a864333d5da" :question/math-academy-id "q-213090" :question/problem "Let $a$ be a positive integer. Construct an expression that gives the last digit of $15a.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $b=15a.$ Note that $b$ is positive. Now, let ${d}_{3},$ ${d}_{2},$ and ${d}_{1}$ be the last three digits of the number $b:$ \n\n$$\nb=…{d}_{3}{d}_{2}{d}_{1}\n$$\n\nThen, $b$ can be written in expanded form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =⋯+100{d}_{3}+10{d}_{2}+{d}_{1} \\\\  & =10(⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the residue of $b$ modulo $10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ≡10(⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0\\cdot (⋯+10{d}_{3}+{d}_{2})+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡0+{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\  & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${d}_{1}$ is the last digit of $b.$\n\nFinally, since $b=15a,$ and \n\n$$\n15≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 15a & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 5a & ≡{d}_{1} &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression that gives the last digit of $15a$ is the following:\n\n$$\n5a\\,\\text{mod}\\,10\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152057 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a090bd2-cdb1-5680-81bc-3cb36de126c4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Last Few Digits of a Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13f843d4-6653-57d0-9b3c-9c37ec913b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412270} {:answer/id #uuid "4deb678c-8d2a-5d5f-ba4b-9d6c6e6d7862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412295} {:answe