due of $-21$ modulo $5$ is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152056 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70cef00-bf25-5423-85ac-2d3a44c68f35" :knowledge-point/title "Modular Residues of Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a19707-be57-5e82-8eb4-0944e0c8696f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412300} {:answer/id #uuid "91840381-efb0-52a9-a878-768f9ce27516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412307} {:answer/id #uuid "a7af7fe3-0c2d-5d34-8fe5-f16f1ad6fe52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412313} {:answer/id #uuid "da42cea3-d702-5d12-bf8f-94a1bc835e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412332} {:answer/id #uuid "e812db0e-640e-54c1-a36a-e2ae29ef8613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75a19707-be57-5e82-8eb4-0944e0c8696f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412300} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ca19ee1-2131-5b73-85ea-31b8d76a7452" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9feebe3a-396b-5d25-94bd-022707c998e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-76976" :question/problem "$-49\\text{ mod }7=$" :question/worked-solution "The residue of $-49$ modulo $7$ is the integer $0\\le r<7$ such that\n\n$$\n-49≡r\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo find the residue $r,$ we need to write $-49$ as an integer multiple of $7,$ plus the residue $r.$\n\nWe note that $-49≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ because\n\n$$\n-49=(-7)\\cdot 7+0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-49$ modulo $7$ is $0.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can use the addition property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49 & ≡-49+0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-49+7\\cdot 7 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡-49+49 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡0 &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-49$ modulo $7$ is $0.$"}]}
